WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.380
If you want to take a break
from all the MCP stuff,

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:06.380
want to go back to your resume,
go back to your projects,

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:09.820
and how this can actually help you
in your job search

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:13.740
is you can build a tool
that proves you can do the job

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.900
you're applying for
before you get the job.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.340
So I think one thing
we were talking about was like,

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:21.580
okay, you have your past experience
and you can say,

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:25.060
here's what I built, here are some projects
I've built, stuff I've worked on.

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:28.000
But since Claude is
such a good research tool,

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.600
you can use it to find out
more about a company,

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:33.300
more about a particular
product area in a company,

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.200
and more about what you might
actually have to do

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:39.280
in that role at that company
before you work there.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:40.280
So let me show you what I did.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:43.680
So I'll go ahead
and I'll show a few more slides.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:44.800
So that's the idea.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.540
You can pick a task
that the job requires.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:53.200
You could have Claude make some mock data
to show what you might do as part of that job.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.400
And then you can actually
just build that.
